  <!-- MBED TLS, COMPILED THE WAY THIS BUILD NEEDS IT - the TLS that cpp-httplib speaks.

       The sources are the submodule's, pinned at a tag and moved by changing a gitlink; nothing here writes
       into src\3rdparty\mbedtls. This file says only WHICH of them are compiled and WITH WHAT, and it says
       what the submodule's own CMake says, so that the two build systems make one library and not two.

       THE LIST IS NAMED FILE BY FILE, in the submodule's order, out of library/CMakeLists.txt (src_crypto,
       src_x509, src_tls: 81 + 9 + 18). A wildcard would be one line and a second authority: library\*.c is
       109 files, the lists are 108, and the odd one is ecp_curves_new.c, which upstream keeps as an empty
       translation unit "only for compatibility with custom build systems". WHEN THE SUBMODULE IS BUMPED,
       re-check this list against those three sets - that is the price of not having a wildcard, and the
       reason for it is that a bump should show which files moved.

       3rdparty/everest and 3rdparty/p256-m are absent on purpose: both drivers are off in the configuration
       this build uses (mbedtls_config.h:749 and :1487 are commented out) and their sources sit wholly inside
       their own #if, so they compile to nothing. Turn either on in oes_mbedtls_config.h and its sources
       belong here too.

       MBEDTLS_USER_CONFIG_FILE is NOT set here: the callers need the same value, or they and the library
       disagree about the size of a context that holds a mutex. It is in ConfigurationDefs.props, beside the
       cpp-httplib macros, and that file says why. -->
